[0m  [2mThe `pipeline.py` script processes server logs and generates a report. It works, but it's a security and maintenance nightmare:
[0m  [2m
[0m  [2m- Credentials and paths are hardcoded
[0m  [2m- SQL queries are built with string formatting — a textbook injection risk
[0m  [2m- All logic is crammed into one function
[0m  [2m- Log parsing is fragile (no regex)
[0m  [2m- No type hints or documentation
[0m  [2m
[0m  [2mRefactor it. Requirements:
[0m  [2m1. Use environment variables for all config (DB path, log file path, credentials)
[0m  [2m2. Fix the SQL injection — use parameterized queries
[0m  [2m3. Break it into well-named functions following Extract → Transform → Load
[0m  [2m4. Use regex for log line parsing
[0m  [2m5. Add type hints and docstrings
[0m  [2m
[0m  [2mThe `report.html` output must still be produced with the same information (error summary, API latency table, active session count). You may rename the file to `pipeline_refactored.py` if you prefer.
